# Cases where the isemail list's own category differs from our reading of the RFCs. Each is listed here with the clause that decides it;
# none is a divergence from a reference implementation. The first run lists the disagreements; this file records each decision.
# Format: isemail id ¦ expected (valid | invalid) ¦ reason
23 ¦ invalid ¦ RFC 3696 section 2: the top-level domain is not all-numeric (the list calls it valid for RFC 5321)
24 ¦ invalid ¦ RFC 3696 section 2: the top-level domain is not all-numeric (the list calls it valid for RFC 5321)
